The root cause of the build failure is a combination of a Kconfig issue and a bug in a header file.

The Kconfig warnings indicate that `CONFIG_MCUBOOT_IMG_MANAGER` is being disabled, despite being set in `prj.conf`. This is likely due to an unsatisfied dependency or a configuration conflict not visible in the provided files. When `CONFIG_MCUBOOT_IMG_MANAGER` is disabled, `CONFIG_IMG_BLOCK_BUF_SIZE` also becomes undefined because its definition depends on `CONFIG_MCUBOOT_IMG_MANAGER`.

The C/C++ compilation error occurs because the header file `include/zephyr/dfu/flash_img.h` unconditionally defines `struct flash_img_context` with a member array `buf` whose size is `CONFIG_IMG_BLOCK_BUF_SIZE`. When this Kconfig option is undefined, the preprocessor leaves `CONFIG_IMG_BLOCK_BUF_SIZE` as-is, and the compiler treats it as an undeclared identifier, causing the build to fail.

The fix is to make the header file more robust by making the problematic struct member conditional. The `buf` member is specific to the `MCUBOOT_IMG_MANAGER` implementation, so it should be enclosed in an `#if defined(CONFIG_MCUBOOT_IMG_MANAGER)` block. This ensures that the header can be included and compiled even when `MCUBOOT_IMG_MANAGER` is not the selected image manager implementation.

include/zephyr/dfu/flash_img.h
